WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.550
Two farms on two continents grow the
same crop for the same European port.

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.810
At the dock, one load goes in tax-free.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.650
The other pays a tariff: a tax on imports.

4
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.270
The rules of world trade
are set by the WTO:

5
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.430
166 members, representing
98 per cent of world trade.

6
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.690
Same crop, same buyers.

7
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.990
So why does one farmer
pay, and the other not?

8
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.950
In this mission, you'll unpack the
tools that open or close a market:

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.490
tariffs, quotas and subsidies.

10
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.650
Then you'll follow trade between
big and smaller economies,

11
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.750
and see what access means
for workers and shoppers.

12
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.730
Your mission: explain why one farmer
sells tax-free in Europe while the other

13
00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.960
pays a tariff.
